Before a dispatch calls its listeners, it roots them all. Blink’s
EventEmitter::DispatchSync() keeps them in a v8::LocalVector of handles
too, and WebKit’s WebExtensionAPIEvent::invokeListenersWithArgument()
copies its list of reference-counted listeners first. And Gecko’s
EventManager holds each callback in a closure, and calls it only after
shouldFire() confirms that its context is still live.

Nothing of a detached world runs in the shared document again.
Blink resets the context in ScriptContext::Invalidate(), Gecko’s
ContentScriptContextChild::close() nukes the sandbox of the content
script, and WebKit’s JSWebExtensionWrapper::finalize() drops the API
object — so a retained function or callback of the old world can’t
act in any of them either.
